Z||000000||wxxo||02-23-2000||05:01 PM||||here's one for yall. i got barely any power and terrible fuel mileage. (100 miles to the tank!) yes i've checked and there isn't a hole in my gas tank! what do you think would cause this. i got an 86 se with a v-6 four speed if that helps any. it is also making a strange sh sh sh sh sound when i give it the gas. im thinking that i've got a cracked manifold. what do yall think?? by the way im still looking to do a coup to fastback conversion on my fiero. if any of you know of anyone with an extra rear end clip from a gt that will work lemme know. thanks! ||||reg||5
Z||000001||mwbackus||02-23-2000||05:35 PM||||Sounds like a clogged cat. convertor to me...||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||02-23-2000||05:40 PM||||I know a bad oxygen sensor can cause similar symptoms too, especially the gas hogging.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||02-23-2000||05:42 PM||||A cracked exhaust manifold should not cause that kind of performance or MPG problems. Sounds are REALLY hard to figure out over the internet... A sound described as "SH" sounds more like a compression leak than an exhaust leak. <P>Kind of a long shot, but here goes:<BR>Last summer a friend of my son's had trouble with her 86 SE. Her boyfriend drove it the 100 miles or so from where they were and stopped by my house. It made a "sh" sound... got really bad mileage... and ran like crap... After looking at it we noticed the sound was coming from a "loose" spark plug. It turned out the ceramic part had separated from the outer metal part. The ceramic part would slid in and out making the gap go from 0 to about 1/2 inch. It was also letting most of the compression out of that cylinder. Her boyfriend put in new plugs and all was well!!!<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000004||Phaeton||02-23-2000||10:25 PM||||When my cat clogged it made the  funny noise by blowing the pressure out where the spring loaded gasket joins the pipe to the manifold, I took off the bolts and dropped the pipe an inch from the manifold and took it for a short test drive.  All the power came back (along with a LOT of noise). ||||reg||1
Z||000005||HotFieroGT||02-23-2000||11:01 PM||||My vote is for the cat. also!||||reg||1
Z||000006||mshill||02-24-2000||12:28 PM||||The same happened to my 86SE in December.  I had a manifold leak and found no exhaust coming out of the tail pipe.  Turned out the cat was melted and clogged and all the exhaust was being forced out the cracked manifold.  Absolutely no power at all.<P>||||reg||1
